sequenceDiagram
    participant SS as FEBSimpleShoppingStrategy
    participant O as FEBOutlet
    participant OI as Outlet inventory
    participant H as FEBHousehold
    participant HI as Household inventory
    participant L as FEBShoppingList
    SS->>O: sellCategory c quantityUpTo q withMoneyUpTo m to h
    O->>OI: quantityLeftTomorrowInCategory c
    Note over O: amount := min(q, available, floor(m / price c))
    O->>OI: take c quantity amount<br/>freshest batches first, never last-day food
    OI-->>O: extracted batches
    alt amount is 0
        O-->>SS: 0
    else amount above 0
        O->>O: purchase := FEBPurchase(h, o, c, amount, amount x price)
        O->>H: receive batches for purchase
        loop each batch
            H->>H: store batch
            Note over H,HI: fridge food goes into fridge up to free space,<br/>the rest moves outside and its shelf life<br/>is scaled to the outside shelf life
            H->>HI: addBatch (merge if same category,<br/>fridge state and remainingDays)
        end
        H->>H: remainingMoney -= price<br/>today addPurchase
        O->>O: today addSale purchase
        O-->>SS: amount
        SS->>L: decreaseNeedOf c by amount<br/>(essential first, then storage)
    end
